      "side": 1,
      "message": "The android.hardware.automotive@libc++fs library has a copy of std::filesystem from libc++. It stops compiling after upgrading libc++ because it depends on libc++ internals that have changed. Rather than try to fix those dependencies, I decided to switch to the official libc++ std::filesystem.\n\nI think it\u0027s a bad idea to tie a bunch of CLs to the overall libc++ update (topic `use-prebuilt-libcxx`), so I instead modified the library to delegate to std::filesystem when `_LIBCPP_VERSION` is newer than what\u0027s in external/libcxx.\n\nDoes this approach make sense to people?\n\nFor reference, some of the internals include:\n - `_LIBCPP_CONSTEXPR_AFTER_CXX11` is removed\n - `std::__is_input_iterator` is removed\n - `__append_forward_unsafe` method in std::string is removed",
